---
import Network from "../../layouts/Network.astro";
---

<Network
  title="ABF Network — Partnerships"
  description="Discover collaboration and partnership opportunities with ABF Network and its different media."
>
  <section class="network-hero">
    <div class="network-container">
      <p class="network-eyebrow">PARTNERSHIPS & COLLABORATION</p>

      <h1>Build projects<br /><span>together.</span></h1>

      <p class="network-intro">
        ABF Network is open to collaborations with organizations in media,
        technology, creative industries and culture.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="network-section" aria-labelledby="collaboration-title">
    <div class="network-container network-two-column">
      <div>
        <p class="network-eyebrow">COLLABORATION</p>
        <h2 id="collaboration-title">Collaborations tailored to each project.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="network-copy">
        <p>
          A partnership can take different forms depending on the project’s objectives
          technical collaboration, technical partnership,
          digital development or media project.
        </p>

        <p>
          ABF Network favors clearly defined collaborations,
          with objectives and roles identified for each party.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="network-section network-section-dark" aria-labelledby="opportunities-title">
    <div class="network-container">
      <div class="network-section-heading">
        <p class="network-eyebrow">OPPORTUNITIES</p>
        <h2 id="opportunities-title">Several ways to collaborate.</h2>
        <p>
          Opportunities depend on the project, its audience and the
          skills or resources required.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="network-partner-grid">
        <article class="network-partner-card">
          <span class="network-card-index">01 / MEDIA</span>
          <h3>Media partnerships</h3>
          <p>
            Editorial collaborations, special operations, content
            and joint projects with other media organizations.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="network-partner-card">
          <span class="network-card-index">02 / TECHNOLOGY</span>
          <h3>Partnerships techniques</h3>
          <p>
            Collaboration around technology, broadcasting,
            digital services and media infrastructure.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="network-partner-card">
          <span class="network-card-index">03 / CREATIVE</span>
          <h3>Creative projects</h3>
          <p>
            Projects combining music, audiovisual, digital creation,
            design or new formats.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="network-partner-card">
          <span class="network-card-index">04 / PROFESSIONAL</span>
          <h3>Professional relations</h3>
          <p>
            Exchanges with companies, agencies, institutions,
            creators and professionals wishing to discover the network.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="network-section" aria-labelledby="network-fit-title">
    <div class="network-container network-feature-grid">
      <div class="network-feature-card">
        <p class="network-eyebrow">THE NETWORK</p>
        <h2 id="network-fit-title">An evolving ecosystem.</h2>
        <p>
          ABF Network projects evolve progressively. New
          media, services and experiences can join the ecosystem
          as it develops.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="network-feature-card">
        <p class="network-eyebrow">OUR PRINCIPLES</p>
        <h2>Collaborations aligned with our identity.</h2>
        <p>
          Partnerships are considered with respect for the network’s independence,
          the identity of its media and the nature of each project.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="network-section network-section-dark" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <div class="network-container network-contact-card">
      <p class="network-eyebrow">START A CONVERSATION</p>

      <h2 id="contact-title">Do you have a project?</h2>

      <p>
        Introduce your project, activity or collaboration proposal.
        Together, we can determine whether it
        fits the ABF Network ecosystem.
      </p>

      <a class="network-contact-button" href="mailto:contact@radioabf.com">
        Contact ABF Network
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Network>

<style>
  .network-hero {
    padding: 112px 0 120px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 82% 18%, rgba(148,163,184,.13), transparent 48%),
      linear-gradient(145deg, #17191e, #090a0c 72%);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);
  }

  .network-eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    color: #aeb4c0;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .24em;
  }

  .network-hero h1 {
    max-width: 920px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(48px, 7.5vw, 104px);
    font-weight: 850;
    line-height: 1.03;
    letter-spacing: -.065em;
  }

  .network-hero h1 span {
    color: #aeb4c0;
  }

  .network-intro {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 34px 0 0;
    color: #b8bdc7;
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 21px);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .network-section {
    padding: 96px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
  }

  .network-section-dark {
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, #111318, #08090b);
  }

  .network-two-column,
  .network-feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 80px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .network-section h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: #f3f4f6;
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.5vw, 62px);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
  }

  .network-copy {
    max-width: 720px;
    color: #b8bdc7;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .network-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }

  .network-section-heading {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .network-section-heading > p:last-child {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    color: #8f96a3;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .network-partner-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .network-partner-card,
  .network-feature-card {
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.025);
  }

  .network-partner-card {
    min-height: 230px;
    padding: 30px;
  }

  .network-card-index {
    color: #8f96a3;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .18em;
  }

  .network-partner-card h3 {
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
    color: #f3f4f6;
    font-size: 23px;
  }

  .network-partner-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #969eaa;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .network-feature-card {
    padding: 38px;
  }

  .network-feature-card h2 {
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 52px);
  }

  .network-feature-card > p:not(.network-eyebrow) {
    max-width: 650px;
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    color: #aeb4c0;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .network-contact-card {
    max-width: 920px;
  }

  .network-contact-card > p:not(.network-eyebrow) {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 24px 0 32px;
    color: #aeb4c0;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .network-contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    min-height: 48px;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #e5e7eb;
    color: #101114;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 750;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform .2s ease;
  }

  .network-contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .network-two-column,
    .network-feature-grid,
    .network-partner-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 38px;
    }

    .network-section {
      padding: 72px 0;
    }

    .network-hero {
      padding: 76px 0 84px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .network-partner-card,
    .network-feature-card {
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .network-hero h1 {
      letter-spacing: -.045em;
    }
  }
</style>